
----- Help -----      (Extended diag messages are OFF)

---- Legend ----
<D:P:S>   Device:Port:System. If omitted, assumes master.

--- Commands ---
? or help                This list.
date                     Show the current date.
clear persistent vars    Clear the persistent variables on the next reboot.
change password          Change your password (requires login).
device holdoff           [on|off]  Sets the master to holdoff devices until all
                         objects in the master are running.  If set to ON, any
                         messages sent to devices in DEFINE_START will be lost,
                         however, this prevents messages from devices being
                         lost before DEFINE_START runs.
disk free                Show the amount of free space on the disk.
dot1x                    [enable|disable|status]  Enable/Disable 802.1x
                         security or display current settings.
echo                     [on|off]  Enables/Disables echo of typed characters.
export config to usb     [front|back]  Exports configuration data to USB media.
export config to backup  Exports configuration data to /backup/config.
export clone to usb      [front|back]  Exports system clone to USB media.
export clone to backup   Exports system clone to /backup/clone.
get device holdoff       Show the state of the master's device holdoff setting.
get duet memory          Display the amount of memory allocated for Duet Java
                         pool.
resetadminpassword       Reset Administrator password.
security help            Show security related commands.
axlink-trace             [enable|disable] [rx|tx|both]  Enables/Disables AXLINK
                         message tracing.
manage firmware          Calculate and display checksums for stored firmware
                         installation files.
import                   [kit|tkn|irl|config]  Import files of specified type
                         from USB media device.
mem                      Shows the amount of available memory.
msg                      on [error|warning|info|debug]|off  Enables/Disables
                         extended diagnostic messages.
date/time                [on|off]  Enables/Disables date and time stamp on the
                         telnet session log.
netlinx log level        Configure the current setting for the NetLinx LOG
                         facility.
off                      [D:P:S or Name,Chan]  Turns off the specified channel.
on                       [D:P:S or Name,Chan]  Turns on the specified channel.
pass                     [D:P:S or Name]  Puts the Session in pass mode to the
                         specified device. Mode is exited by ++ ESC ESC.
                         Display Format is set by ++ ESC n. If n is A,
                         format=ASCII, D=Decimal,H=Hex.
ping                     [address]  Pings an address. Address may be an IP or
                         URL.
pulse                    [D:P:S or Name, Chan]  Pulses the specified channel.
pwd                      Lists out the current working directory.
reboot                   [D:P:S|cold|warm]  Reboots the specified device.
                         Options:
                           D:P:S  Reboots the device.
                           cold  Reboots the master.
                           warm  Restarts the master process.
renew dhcp               Renews the current DHCP lease.
report firmware          Calculate and display checksums for stored firmware
                         installation files.
report netlinx           Calculate and display a checksum for the currently
                         installed Netlinx code.
reset ntp                Resets NTP servers to default servers.
reset factory            Resets configuration back to factory defaults. It will
                         also reboot the device.
route mode               Set the Master-Master route mode.
send command             [D:P:S or Name,Command]  Sends the specified command
                         to the device. The Command uses NetLinx string syntax.
                         Examples:
                           send_command 1:1:1,"'This is a test',13,10"
                           send_command RS232_1,"'This is a test',13,10"
send string              [D:P:S or Name,String]  Sends the specified string to
                         the device.
send level               [D:P:S,LEVEL#,VALUE]  Sends the specified level event
                         to the device.
                         Ex: send level 1:1:1,3,7
set date                 Set the current date.
set dns                  [D:P:S]  Setup the DNS configuration of a device.
set duet memory          Set the amount of memory allocated for Duet Java pool.
set ftp port             Enables/Disables the IP port listened to for FTP
                         connections.
set http port            Sets the IP port listened to for HTTP connections.
set https port           Sets the IP port listened to for HTTPS connections.
set https redirect       Sets the HTTPS redirect flag. All HTTP requests will
                         be redirected to HTTPS.
clear https redirect     Clear the HTTPS redirect flag.
show https redirect      Show HTTPS redirect status.
set icsp tcp timeout     Sets the timeout period for ICSP and i!-WebControl TCP
                         connections.
set icslan               Sets the ICSLan port values.
get icslan               Displays the ICSLan port values.
get leases               Displays the leases on ICSLan port.
set ip                   [D:P:S]  Setup the IP configuration of a device.
set ipv6                 [D:P:S]  Setup the IPv6 configuration of a device.
set log count            Sets the number of entries allowed in the message log.
set queue size           Set the max entry count for various process queues.
set ssh port             Sets the IP port listened to for SSH connections.
set telnet port          Sets the IP port listened to for telnet connections.
set threshold            Sets the master's internal message thresholds.
set timeline loopcnt     Sets Sets the master's timeline/event max loopcount.
set time                 Set the current time.
set udp bc rate          Set UDP broadcast rate.  A broadcast message is sent
                         by the master to allow devices to discover the master.
                         This command allows the broadcast frequency to be
                         changed or eliminate the broadcast message.
set url                  [D:P:S]  Setup the initiated connection list URLs of a
                         device.
set system number        Sets the system number for the Master.
set notify throttle      Sets the M2M notification throttle level (1-10).
show combine             Displays a list of devices, levels, and channels that
                         are currently combined.
time                     Show the current time.
url list                 [D:P:S]  Display the initiated connection list URLs of
                         a device.
show log                 [start]  Display the message log. <start> specifies
                         message to begin the display. 'all' will display all
                         messages.
start log                [on|off]  Enables/Disables the start up log.
show start log           [start]  Display the start up log. <start> specifies
                         message to begin the display. 'all' will display all
                         messages.
usb log                  [front|back] [enable|disable]  Enables/Disables log
                         writes to USB media.
get audit status         Displays disk free space percentage, log daemon status.
list audit files         Display filenames of all locally stored audit files.
show audit               [filename] [tail]  Display today's audit records.
                         Optional filename can be specified to display previous
                         audit logs. Number of lines to tail can be specified.
clear audit              Removes all locally stored audit files.
edit audit security      Display / edit security settings for remote syslog
                         servers.
list audit servers       Lists all remote syslog servers that receive audit
                         messages.
add audit server         [D:P:P]  Adds a remote syslog server for audit
                         messages.
                         D - IP address or hostname for the remote server.
                         P - port number (such as 514, 2514, 6514, 10514, etc.
                         P - protocol (either UDP, TCP, or RELP).
remove audit server      [D:P:P] Removes a remote syslog server for audit
                         messages.
                         D - IP address or hostname for the remote server.
                         P - port number (such as 514, 2514, 6514, 10514, etc.
                         P - protocol (either UDP, TCP, or RELP).
export audit to usb      [front|back]  Exports all locally stored audit files
                         to USB media.
export audit to backup   Exports all locally stored audit files to
                         /backup/audit.
clean disk               Deletes files in user directory and the NetLinx
                         prog.tkn file.
list                     [-sda] [path]  List a directory as specified by
                         <path>. The root directory is /opt/amx/.
                         Example: list /opt/amx/user.
                         Options:
                           [-s] short (name only)
                           [-d] directories only
                           [-sd] directory name only
                           [-a] all
show buffers             Displays current message buffer usage for various
                         tasks.
show max buffers         Displays message buffer high water mark for various
                         tasks.
clear max buffers        Clears message buffer high water mark for various
                         tasks.
msg stats                Displays statistics on number of messages processed in
                         last 10 seconds.
dns list                 [D:P:S]  Show the DNS configuration of a device.
tod adjustments          # of times Linux was different than the clock chip.
get ip                   [D:P:S]  Show the IP configuration of a device.
zeroconf                 [enable|disable|status] ZeroConfig setting.
java security            [enable|disable|status] Java Security Manager setting.
ndp                      [enable|disable|status] NDP Beacon setting.
ip status                Provides information about NetLinx IP Connections.
program info             Displays a list of program modules loaded.
program                  [enable|disable|status] NetLinx Program run setting.
show mem                 Displays the memory usage for all memory types.
ipdd                     [enable|disable|status] IP Device Discovery setting.
auto locate              [enable|disable|status Enable/disable master auto
                         locate.
boot status              Retrieve the current boot status.
get platform info        Retrieve the platform info.
show watchdog            View Watchdog Manager monitors
set cac field            Set CAC Field Validation [SAN|SCN].
show remote              Displays the Remote Device List (Master-Master).
show notify              Displays the Notify Device List (Master-Master).
icspmon                  [enable|disable][port]  Enable/disable ICSP monitoring
                         on the specified IP port.
physical status          Displays physical status LED indicators.
dipswitch                Displays current dipswitch value.
device status            <D:P:S>[/v]  Displays info about the specified device.
ds                       See device status.
show device              [D:P:S][/min][/all]  Displays a list of devices
                         connected and attributes.
sd                       See show device.
show system              [<S>][/min]  Displays a list of devices in a system.
cpu usage                Displays the total CPU usage.
log format               Change log format settings.
show route               [/v]  Displays the Master's routing information.
show tcp                 [/v][/all]  Displays a list of active TCP connections.
get device traffic       Gets Diagnostic information about device side traffic
device debug             Turns the device side traffic debug messages on or off.
set device reboot        Set the fault response to a NI device side failure
mail status              Displays mail lib performance.
mail reset               Reset the mail service.
